{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1784624078,"nonce":"/Kd/OCAxWK7s1SF0y1CxUhcrrng=","title":"Shared service — failure semantics","message":"## Parent\nEpic 01c81a5\n\n## What to build\nFailure handling for Shared services. Startup flake (fails to become ready the first time, nothing written yet) → bounded auto-retry of the service Pod → exhausted → fail the Run. Mid-run death of a previously-healthy service → FAIL-CLOSED: opt-in Steps fail with an unbound-dependency diagnostic, descendants cascade (ADR-0027), and the engine does NOT auto-rerun (no auto-forking of a Take); non-opt-in Steps proceed untouched.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] Startup failure → bounded auto-retry of the service Pod, then Run failure\n- [ ] Mid-run death → opt-in Steps fail + descendants cascade; NO auto-rerun / no Take fork\n- [ ] Non-opt-in Steps are unaffected by a service death\n- [ ] Tests covering both the startup-flake and mid-run-death paths\n\n## Blocked by\nSlice 2 (58646c1)","files":null}]}